{"step_index":99,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T05:52:11Z","thinking":"Begin by defining the visual style for the notification bar within the stylesheet, including a gradient background and blur effect to achieve the desired aesthetic. This addresses the specified visual styling requirements for the notification element. The defined styles are now ready to be applied.\n\n\nExamining the provided HTML structure, the notification bell button and the notification bar elements are identified for integration.  These elements are now being added to the appropriate sections within `index.html`, specifically within the header's right-side actions and directly below the header.\n\n\nNow analyzing the HTML structure of the notification bar's internal elements.  Specifically, extracting the content related to the urgency tag, message, and action button for dynamic update capabilities. Considering how to implement a state management system to handle these elements.\n\n\nFocus is now on integrating the notification bar's functionality, including previous/next alert navigation, auto-cycling, and dismissal features. The HTML structure of these controls is being analyzed to ensure proper event handling and dynamic updates of the notification counter. The auto-cycle countdown line's implementation is also under consideration.\n\n\nAnalyzing how to manage the selected interval and persist it across sessions using the local storage mechanism. This includes implementing event listeners for the interval selection dropdown to capture user preferences. Considering the structure for storing and retrieving the selected interval from local storage.\n\n\nNow focusing on incorporating the interval selection and desktop notification elements into the notification bar's HTML structure.  Event handlers need to be set up for the dropdown and notification button. Considering how to dynamically update the interval display and handle user interaction.\n\nThe pending reminder trigger button is being integrated. Considering how this button will interface with the notification system's logic to immediately display a test alert.\n\n\nNow examining the data structures within the application's state to understand how alerts will be generated and managed. Specifically, analyzing the logic for building pending work alerts based on assignment due dates, subject attendance, and exam dates. Determining how alert objects will be structured, and the details each will contain. The structure of the alert objects and how the UI component will render it is under consideration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add styles for notification bar, ticker progress line, and drawer","EndLine":115,"Instruction":"Insert notification bar and progress line styles into styles.css","ReplacementContent":".mobile-nav-btn.active span:first-child {\n  transform: scale(1.18);\n  filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 8px rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.6));\n}\n\n/* ========================================================\n   🔔 NOTIFICATION BAR & PENDING WORK TICKER\n======================================================== */\n.notification-bar {\n  background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(30, 27, 75, 0.94) 0%, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.95) 50%, rgba(88, 28, 135, 0.9) 100%);\n  backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(129, 140, 248, 0.25);\n  box-shadow: 0 6px 20px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);\n  transition: all 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);\n}\n\n.notification-bar.urgent-alert {\n  background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(88, 28, 28, 0.96) 0%, rgba(30, 27, 75, 0.94) 50%, rgba(88, 28, 135, 0.92) 100%);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.45);\n}\n\n.notification-bar.warning-alert {\n  background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(88, 55, 20, 0.96) 0%, rgba(20, 30, 60, 0.94) 50%, rgba(50, 20, 80, 0.92) 100%);\n  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.45);\n}\n\n.notification-progress {\n  height: 2px;\n  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #f59e0b, #ec4899, #6366f1);\n  transition: width 0.1s linear;\n}\n\n.pulse-badge {\n  animation: pulseBadge 2s infinite;\n}\n\n@keyframes pulseBadge {\n  0%, 100% {\n    transform: scale(1);\n    opacity: 1;\n  }\n  50% {\n    transform: scale(1.08);\n    opacity: 0.85;\n  }\n}\n","StartLine":105,"TargetContent":".mobile-nav-btn.active span:first-child {\n  transform: scale(1.18);\n  filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 8px rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.6));\n}\n","TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\DELL\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\student-survival-app\\styles.css","toolAction":"Updating styles.css","toolSummary":"Add notification bar CSS"}}]}
